---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Methodology · Sutton Hills Research Partners">
<style>
  .page-header { padding: 3rem 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border); margin-bottom:2rem; }
  .content-section { padding: 1.5rem 0; }
  .content-section p { max-width:700px; line-height:1.8; }
  .step-list { list-style:none; counter-reset:steps; padding:0; margin:1.5rem 0; }
  .step-list li { counter-increment:steps; padding:1rem 0 1rem 3.5rem; position:relative; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .step-list li::before { content:counter(steps, decimal-leading-zero); position:absolute; left:0; top:1rem; font-family:var(--font-heading); font-size:1.5rem; color:var(--color-accent); font-weight:700; }
</style>

<div class="container">
  <div class="page-header">
    <h1>Our Research Methodology</h1>
    <p style="color:var(--color-muted);margin-top:0.5rem;">How we select topics, gather evidence, and produce our reports.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;">Process Overview</h2>
    <ol class="step-list">
      <li><strong>Topic Selection:</strong> We identify research gaps based on recurring questions from institutional buyers and market intelligence.</li>
      <li><strong>Evidence Collection:</strong> Analysts gather published data, vendor documentation, user reviews, and industry submissions.</li>
      <li><strong>Evaluation:</strong> Evidence is assessed against our pre-published criteria. Each source is rated for reliability.</li>
      <li><strong>Review:</strong> Draft reports undergo peer review by at least one named external reviewer.</li>
      <li><strong>Publication:</strong> Reports are published with full disclosure of limitations and evidence quality ratings.</li>
      <li><strong>Correction:</strong> When new evidence emerges, we update reports and document all changes publicly.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;">Evidence Quality Framework</h2>
    <p>We rate evidence across four tiers:</p>
    <ul style="margin-top:1rem; padding-left:1.5rem;">
      <li style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;"><strong>Tier A — Primary Data:</strong> Direct quantitative results, audit outcomes, verified case studies.</li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;"><strong>Tier B — Expert Testimony:</strong> Statements from recognised authorities, peer-reviewed academic work.</li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;"><strong>Tier C — Secondary Sources:</strong> Industry analyses, analyst firm reports, trade publications.</li>
      <li><strong>Tier D — Vendor-Provided:</strong> Marketing materials, white papers, product documentation (rated as lowest weight).</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>
</BaseLayout>
